  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>805</x>
      <y>63</y>
      <w>182</w>
      <h>112</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>World is a 2D Grid
and organizes the pieces into
grid cells and is the top-level
container for Grid Cells
which contain n pieces. World 
inderstands the dimensions
of the game and represents the
sturcutre of where pieces
live.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1050</x>
      <y>525</y>
      <w>21</w>
      <h>21</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>#
bg=yellow
layer=1</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>952</x>
      <y>329</y>
      <w>154</w>
      <h>70</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>World is a 2-D Grid of cells.
Each cell has n pieces.
Pieces know what their
cooridate is, but don't know
anything about the world.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>21</x>
      <y>357</y>
      <w>266</w>
      <h>49</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>/iMovable/
--
/+Set_Location (World_2D):Grid_Coordinate/
/+Set_Location (World_2D,Direction,Grid_Coordinate,Valid)/
</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>245</x>
      <y>245</y>
      <w>217</w>
      <h>98</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Might need to create specific named
associations for specific kind of
pieces. For example, a player piece
and an array of monsters. In general,
the design is to have an association
to many kinds of pieces. Let the
implementation figure it out.
*This is why assoc. is not given a role name*</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>168</x>
      <y>70</y>
      <w>189</w>
      <h>147</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>UML Note
Dependecy usage ---&gt;
loose coupling via parameter coupling.
i.e. clas shows up in a parameter
of a class method.
Static class diagrams should
only have persistent relationships.
Temporal relationships via class
parameters are relaized throush
dependecy relationships.
</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>378</x>
      <y>77</y>
      <w>189</w>
      <h>161</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Quasi builder pattern
Game controller creates pieces
at start of game. Keeps
association to control them

Might need to create specific named
associations for specific kind of
pieces. For example, a player piece
and an array of monsters. In general,
the design is to have an association
to many kinds of pieces. Let the
implementation figure it out.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
